# Rust build output
target/
**/target/

# Runtime state. Atlas generates everything under data/ on first run — notes,
# state, the vault, logs, the single-instance lock, the self-work build
# sandboxes, and per-install secrets like the recovery key. None of it is
# source: tests build their own data dirs in temp, and the app recreates this
# tree on run. It was committed by accident in the handed-over baseline and
# churned the working tree on every run; it does not belong in the repo.
atlas/data/
data/
# ...except a fixture that copies somebody else's layout: an X archive keeps
# its files under its own `data/` (29 Sep 2026 -- the folder form of the X
# fixture was ignored by the line above and never reached git, so the test
# that reads it failed on every fresh checkout).
!atlas/tests/fixtures/social/exports/x_archive/data/

# Local logs and OS cruft
*.log
.DS_Store

# The phone apps' build output. The Rust core for each phone is built into
# rustlib/ by the build (mobile/build-android.sh, .github/workflows/ios.yml);
# the Xcode project is generated from project.yml on the cloud Mac.
atlas/mobile/android/.gradle/
atlas/mobile/android/build/
atlas/mobile/android/app/build/
atlas/mobile/android/app/.cxx/
atlas/mobile/android/app/src/main/rustlib/
atlas/mobile/android/local.properties
atlas/mobile/ios/rustlib/
atlas/mobile/ios/*.xcodeproj/
# Signing keys never belong in the repository.
*.p12
*.p8
*.jks
*.keystore
*.mobileprovision
*.pass

# Written by Atlas on each machine (Settings page); never shipped.
atlas/config/settings.yaml
